.Dd January 29, 2026
.Dt LIBBC 3
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm libbc
.Nd arbitrary precision arithmetic library
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In num.h
.Ft bc_num *
.Fn bc_new "void"
.Ft void
.Fn bc_free "bc_num *n"
.Ft bc_num *
.Fn bc_add "bc_num *a" "bc_num *b"
.Ft bc_num *
.Fn bc_sub "bc_num *a" "bc_num *b"
.Ft bc_num *
.Fn bc_mul "bc_num *a" "bc_num *b"
.Ft bc_num *
.Fn bc_div "bc_num *a" "bc_num *b"
.Ft bc_num *
.Fn bc_mod "bc_num *a" "bc_num *b"
.Ft bc_num *
.Fn bc_pow "bc_num *a" "bc_num *b"
.Ft bc_num *
.Fn bc_dup "bc_num *src"
.Te
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library provides arbitrary precision integer arithmetic.
It uses a base-100 representation for internal storage.
.Ss Memory Management
.Fn bc_new
allocates a new number initialized to zero.
.Fn bc_free
frees the memory associated with a number.
.Fn bc_dup
creates a deep copy of a number.
.Ss Arithmetic
All arithmetic functions return a new
.Vt bc_num *
and do not modify their arguments.
The caller must free the result.
.Bl -tag -width "bc_pow"
.It Fn bc_add "a" "b"
Returns
.Va a + b .
.It Fn bc_sub "a" "b"
Returns
.Va a - b .
.It Fn bc_mul "a" "b"
Returns
.Va a * b .
.It Fn bc_div "a" "b"
Returns
.Va a / b .
.It Fn bc_mod "a" "b"
Returns
.Va a % b .
.It Fn bc_pow "a" "b"
Returns
.Va a ^ b .
.El
.Ss Comparison & Utils
.Fn bc_compare
returns -1 if a < b, 0 if a == b, and 1 if a > b.
.Fn bc_is_zero
returns 1 if the number is zero, 0 otherwise.
.Fn bc_is_neg
returns 1 if the number is negative.
.Fn bc_canonicalize
removes leading/trailing zeros (internal use mostly).
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
#include "num.h"

void example(void) {
    bc_num *a = bc_from_long(10);
    bc_num *b = bc_from_long(20);
    bc_num *c = bc_add(a, b);

    // c is 30
    bc_print(c); 
    printf("\\n");

    bc_free(a);
    bc_free(b);
    bc_free(c);
}
.Ed
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Arithmetic functions return a pointer to the result, or
.Dv NULL
on error (e.g., division by zero, though currently `bc` handles zero division by printing error and returning 0).
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bc 1 ,
.Xr dc 1
